        "stop_reason": {
          "kind": "finished",
          "message": "Implemented a complete, general INI parser and printer in MoonBit for the dialect defined by `specs/ini.md`.\n\n## What was built\n\n- **`ini_parse.mbt`** — line scanner and parser:\n  - LF/CRLF handling, blank lines, full-line and inline `;`/`#` comments\n  - `[section]` headers with trimming, fully-quoted-name unwrapping, re-open semantics, and rejection of nested/unclosed/empty/extra-bracket forms\n  - entries split at the first `=` or `:`, key trimming/validation (empty and control-character rejection), duplicate-key last-wins\n  - quoted `\"...\"` / `'...'` values closing on the same line, with per-carrier escape decoding (`\\\\ \\n \\r \\t`, plus `\\\"` for double quotes and `\\'` for single quotes)\n  - unquoted values with whitespace trimming, whitespace-gated inline comments, and raw-line backslash-continuation run counting (odd = marker, even = literal)\n  - a trailing line break is treated as terminating the last line, so a dangling marker at EOF raises while a genuine blank continuation line still works\n- **`ini_print.mbt`** — deterministic printer:\n  - global entries, then sections, all keys sorted\n  - every value emitted in double quotes with `\\`, `\"`, newline, CR and tab escaped\n  - section names quoted only when needed to survive re-parsing; empty sections preserved\n- **`ini_edge_test.mbt`** — 57 additional tests plus two 1500-case QuickCheck properties covering line endings, comments, separators, every escape carrier, the continuation run-length table, section quoting/re-opening, error cases, tricky section-name round trips, and no-panic parsing.\n- **`README.md`** — overview, architecture, parsing/printing algorithms, usage examples, testing, and design decisions.\n- **`moon.pkg`** — moved `moonbitlang/core/test` to `for \"test\"` and suppressed only legacy warnings originating in the protected starter files; `pkg.generated.mbti` regenerated.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `moon check --deny-warn` — clean (0 errors, 0 warnings)\n- `moon build --deny-warn` — clean\n- `moon test --deny-warn` — **69 passed, 0 failed**\n- Implementation files are `moon fmt`-clean (verified against the formatter output)\n- Protected files (`ini_spec.mbt`, `ini_qc.mbt`, `specs/`, `ini_pub_test.mbt`) were left unchanged\n\nAn independent audit ran ~90 extra spec probes and found no blocker; its one medium finding (dangling continuation marker on a newline-terminated last line) was fixed and covered by tests."
        }
