          "kind": "finished",
          "message": "All work is complete and validated. Here's what I built.\n\n## Implementation\n\nEight focused modules in the root `ini` package (all well under the 1000-line limit):\n\n| File | Role |\n|---|---|\n| [error.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\error.mbt) | `ParseError` (`pub(all) suberror`) + `fail_at`, which reports the 1-based line |\n| [text.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\text.mbt) | blank class, trimming, line splitting, inline-comment cutting, trailing-backslash counting |\n| [escape.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\escape.mbt) | `Carrier` (unquoted/double/single) and per-carrier escape decoding |\n| [value.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\value.mbt) | quoted-value scanning (same-line closing quote) + text-after-quote check |\n| [entry.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\entry.mbt) | first-`=`/`:` separator, key validation, unquoted values and continuations |\n| [section.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\section.mbt) | `[name]` extraction, quote-pair stripping, nested-bracket rejection |\n| [parser.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\parser.mbt) | the line scanner / document assembly (`parse`) |\n| [printer.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\printer.mbt) | `print` — double-quoted values, representable section headers |\n\nKey design point: continuation, comment cutting and trimming all run on **raw** text and escapes are decoded exactly once at the end, so `\\\\` (escaped literal) and a trailing `\\` (marker) stay distinguishable; the whole odd/even run table (`1`–`4` backslashes) falls out of counting the run.\n\n## Validation\n\n`moon check`: **0 errors**, and every warning belongs to the protected files (`ini_spec.mbt`, `ini_qc.mbt`, `ini_pub_test.mbt`, `moon.pkg`); none from my code. `moon test`: **87/87 pass**.\n\n- [ini_edge_test.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\ini_edge_test.mbt) — 73 cases derived from `specs/ini.md`: both separators, first-separator-wins, duplicate keys, section re-opening, quoted/quoted-section names, every escape carrier, the run table, CRLF, continuation text-vs-syntax, unicode incl. surrogate pairs, git/systemd/php shapes, and one rejection test per malformed form.\n- [ini_fuzz_test.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\ini_fuzz_test.mbt) — exhaustively parses all 22,621 strings of length ≤ 4 over `[ ] = : ; # \" ' \\ ␠ a ␊`, requiring each to raise or to print into text that parses back equal.\n\nAn independent audit (subagent) confirmed rule-by-rule conformance and no panic risk (its own 30k randomized probe over `\\r`, NUL, DEL, CJK, emoji found no trap). It flagged one real ambiguity — a continuation marker followed only by the file's final line break. Since this repo's test style always ends fixtures with a trailing newline, I changed `split_lines` so the text after the final break is not a line: `k=v\\` is now rejected with or without a trailing newline, while a marker may still join a blank line.\n\n## Documentation\n\n[README.md](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\README.md) documents the pipeline, the filter/comment/escape rules, printing strategy, usage with error handling, the test suite, and both limitations no INI spelling can fix (a hand-built `Doc` with keys like `;a` or `a=b`, and section names containing brackets, cannot round-trip because the dialect has no way to quote them — `parse` can never produce such keys).\n\n`ini_spec.mbt`, `ini_qc.mbt`, `ini_pub_test.mbt` and `specs/` are byte-identical to their originals (`moon fmt` rewrites `ini_spec.mbt`, so I restored it afterwards and verified the file)."
